SUMMARY:From Appreciation to Connoisseurship
DESCRIPTION:In a world of constant noise\, listening with interest\, intent and without interruption is a phenomenal skill. \nThis interactive workshop offers a friendly\, accessible introduction to Hindustani art music for listeners with little or no prior exposure. Rather than approaching the tradition through rules and terminology alone\, the session teaches participants how to listen\, through live demonstration\, guided listening exercises\, and conversation. What actually happens\, moment to moment\, within a Hindustani performance? \nParticipants will pick up some of the tradition’s fundamental concepts and forms\, learning to identify the musical elements at work and to appreciate the choices a performer makes in real time. The focus is on building the ear of an engaged\, informed listener. No prior musical knowledge is required; simply a passion for learning and an interest in the art. \nSchedule:\n\n\nSaturday\, 3 Oct. | 3–7 pm\n3:00–4:30 pm: Session 1\n4:30–5:00 pm: Tea Break\n5:00–7:00 pm: Session 2 \nSunday\, 4 Oct. | 10 am–1:30 pm\n10:00–11:30 am: Session 3\n11:30–11:45 am: Tea Break\n11:45 am–1:30 pm: Session 4 \nPushkar Lele will have a performance on Oct. 3 and 4. More details here. \n\n\n\n\nUnderstanding the Fundamentals of Hindustani Vocal Music\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdN6qZT6coLwGbDvgLsGbbPzjHO7Kcn4IISkkplTjRcHtHP6A/viewform?usp=dialog)\n*Facilitator*: Pushkar Lele\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Workshops
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/from-appreciation-to-connoisseurship/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Workshops
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_FATC.jpg
END:VEVENT
