UID:95421-1791138600-1791144000@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Gombe
DESCRIPTION:This evening brings together three short films\, followed by a conversation between filmmakers Hansa Thapliyal and Paromita Vohra. Each film turns an intimate lens on questions of art\, choice\, and connection. \nThe Outside In\n25m 03s | 2019 | English\, Marathi with English Subtitles\nTwo dollmakers\, working with simple\, discarded materials\, gently loosen our resistance to empathy. The film collaborates with them and their dolls\, blurring the line between what lies outside us and within. \nKya Hai Ye Samjhauta\n9m | 2024 | Hindi with English Subtitles\nBorn from twelve caseworkers’ recordings across rural Uttar Pradesh\, this film uses scraps of cloth\, needle and thread\, and the timbre of human voices to explore women’s choices in the face of domestic violence. This film looks at the word samjhauta and asks: do you make your terms? \nDuniya Kee Raunak\n19m 40s | 2026 | Telugu\, Marathi\, Hindi with English Subtitles\nMust a television screen decide what our lives will be like? Little Mansoor steps beyond his window to befriend the world outside. Blending shadow puppetry\, theatre\, and stop motion\, the film is a tribute to the earliest\, most playful histories of cinema. \nPlease Note: Children under 16 are to be accompanied by an adult. \nVenue: Seminar Halls \n\n\nBecause Dolls\, like Gods\, Have Much to Say to Us\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScBrV5RALRmFsr-5nZ7FyXXUStrTiDI0Fq1FPXy3AQXLCowaA/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Hansa Thapliyal\, Paromita Vohra\n*Event Categories*: Culture\, Film\, Heritage
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/gombe/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Culture,Film,Heritage
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_GB-copy.jpg
END:VEVENT
