UID:95453-1791226800-1791231300@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:The Belle of Amherst
DESCRIPTION:The Belle of Amherst by William Luce\, written in 1976\, is a play based on the life of American poet Emily Dickinson. It was first performed by Julie Harris\, who won a Tony for her role\, in 1977. The story\, narrated by the eccentric Emily herself\, liberally interspersed with her sublime poetry\, is a truly soulful journey for both the character and her audience. Susan George will do a dramatised reading of the play. \nImage Credit\nThe portrait of Emily Dickinson is from the only currently authenticated photograph\, a daguerreotype ca. 1847 in the Amherst College Archives & Special Collections. \nVenue: Library\n\n\nA Dramatised Reading on the Life and Work of Emily Dickinson\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Performer*: Susan George\n*Event Categories*: Literature\, Performing Arts\, Poetry\, Theatre
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-belle-of-amherst/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Literature,Performing Arts,Poetry,Theatre
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ThumbnailBOA.jpg
END:VEVENT
