SUMMARY:Moksha Mudra
DESCRIPTION:\nThis Bharatanatyam production traces the parallel cycles of women and the earth\, each unfolding through the turn of the seasons. As the earth moves through its changing forms\, its female protagonists move through their own inner seasons\, carrying turmoil that mirrors the natural world around them before dissolving into liberation. \nThrough evocative movement\, music\, and storytelling\, the work moves between distinct narratives: the grace of Amrapali\, the devotion of Radha\, the resilience of Sita\, the courage of Rani Lakshmibai\, and the environmental legacy of Amrita Devi. Each episode draws out a different facet of feminine strength and transformation\, building toward a single\, layered portrait of endurance across time. \n\nCredits:\nChoreography: Minal Prabhu\n\nMusic Production: Gayatri Sriram\n\nLighting Design: Keerti Kumar \n\n\n\nSupported by:\n\n\nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nA Woman’s Journey from Turmoil to Liberation\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfJZNEYIFsK7berdBCfMs-5rj4gi0uOXKv7AjXToIn-cS_G2Q/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performers*: Mudrika Foundation\n*Event Categories*: Dance\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/moksha-mudra/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Dance,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail-15-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
