SUMMARY:Pomp and Circumstance
DESCRIPTION: \nThere is always more to a musician than just their music. \nThis talk uncovers the life of Harikeshanallur Dr. L. Muthiah Bhagavatar (1877–1945)\, a flamboyant and larger-than-life figure who found joy in every form of expression available to him. He was a renowned musician\, a prolific composer\, a consummate Harikatha performer\, a well-regarded teacher\, and the author of a treatise on Carnatic music theory. \nTrained first as a Carnatic musician\, Bhagavatar soon turned to Harikatha\, finding in its blend of storytelling\, song\, and stagecraft a fuller outlet for his gifts\, quickly becoming one of its most popular exponents. As an important figure at the Mysore court\, under the patronage of King Krishnaraja Wodeyar\, he composed one hundred and eight songs in praise of Goddess Chamundi\, each one a fresh attempt at devotion. At the invitation of Maharani Sethu Parvathy Bai\, he later moved to the Travancore Palace\, where he became the first principal of the Trivandrum Music College\, turning his private joy in music into a public institution for teaching it. \nEven scholarship\, for Bhagavatar\, became another register of expression. He was the first musician to be awarded a doctorate\, for his thesis\, Sangita Kalpadrumam. Published only after his death\, his theoretical work was born of the same curiosity that drove his performances. Across his lifetime he composed more than four hundred songs in multiple languages and introduced around twenty new ragas into the Carnatic tradition. In 1920\, he founded a gurukula\, the Tyagaraja Sangita Vidyalaya\, in Madurai\, ensuring that this capacity for joyful reinvention would outlive him\, carried forward by students such as Madurai Mani Iyer. \nPresented by:\n \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nThe Life of Harikeshanallur Dr. L. Muthiah Bhagavatar\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScV0Ar_ipmdsCkwEGsoAluVrSrCS38Bibkc16k39pvu24MEvg/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speaker*: V. Sriram\n*Event Categories*: Biography\, Culture\, Heritage\, History\, Music\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/pomp-and-circumstance/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Biography,Culture,Heritage,History,Music,Society
